-- title:
--   §7.2.2, p. 30 — every run of Algorithm 2 (Semi-APGM) is a run of the semi-implicit scheme (115)
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a real Hilbert space, $\mu\ge0$, $L>0$, $\nabla h:V\to V$ a map and $g:V\to\mathbb R\cup\{+\infty\}$ with domain $D$. Let $(\alpha_k,\gamma_k,x_k,y_k,w_k,v_k)$ be generated by Algorithm 2 (Semi-APGM): $\gamma_0>0$ and, for every $k$, $\alpha_k>0$ with $L\alpha_k^2=\gamma_k(1+\alpha_k)$,
--   $$\gamma_{k+1}=\frac{\gamma_k+\mu\alpha_k}{1+\alpha_k},\quad y_k=\frac{x_k+\alpha_kv_k}{1+\alpha_k},\quad w_k=\frac{\gamma_kv_k+\mu\alpha_ky_k}{\gamma_k+\mu\alpha_k},$$
--   $$x_{k+1}=\operatorname{prox}_{g/L}\big(y_k-\tfrac1L\nabla h(y_k)\big),\qquad v_{k+1}=w_k+\frac{\gamma_k}{\gamma_{k+1}}\,\frac{x_{k+1}-y_k}{\alpha_k}.$$
--   Then $(x_k,y_k,v_k,\gamma_k)$ satisfies the semi-implicit scheme (115): for every $k$,
--   $$\frac{y_k-x_k}{\alpha_k}=v_k-y_k,\qquad x_{k+1}=S_f(y_k),\qquad \frac{v_{k+1}-v_k}{\alpha_k}=\frac{\mu}{\gamma_k}(y_k-v_{k+1})-\frac{1}{\gamma_k}\mathcal G_f(y_k),\qquad \frac{\gamma_{k+1}-\gamma_k}{\alpha_k}=\mu-\gamma_{k+1},$$
--   where $\mathcal G_f(y_k)=L(y_k-x_{k+1})$.
--
--   This is the statement that Algorithm 2 "summarizes" (115): it lets every estimate proved for (115) be applied to the algorithm. The $v$-update matches because of the step-size relation $L\alpha_k^2=\gamma_k(1+\alpha_k)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Only $\nabla h$ enters the scheme, so no class assumption on $h$ or $g$ is needed. The prox is the predicate of the definitions file (a minimiser over $\operatorname{dom}g$).
-- source:
--   Luo & Chen, arXiv:1909.03145v4, §7.2.2, (115) and Algorithm 2, p. 30

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NAGFlow_APGM_Setting

namespace NAGFlow.APGM

/-- Algorithm 2 is the semi-implicit scheme (115) (Luo & Chen, arXiv:1909.03145v4, §7.2.2, p. 30).
Let `0 ≤ μ` and `0 < L`. Every run `(α, γ, x, y, w, v)` of Algorithm 2 (Semi-APGM, with `γ₀ > 0`,
`α_k > 0`, `Lα_k² = γ_k(1 + α_k)`, `η = 1/L`) satisfies (115): for every `k`,
`(y_k − x_k)/α_k = v_k − y_k`, `x_{k+1} = S_f(y_k)`,
`(v_{k+1} − v_k)/α_k = (μ/γ_k)(y_k − v_{k+1}) − (1/γ_k)G_f(y_k)` with `G_f(y_k) = L(y_k − x_{k+1})`, and
`(γ_{k+1} − γ_k)/α_k = μ − γ_{k+1}`. -/
theorem algorithm_2_eq_115 {V : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V]
    (gradh : V → V) (g : V → ℝ) (D : Set V) (μ L : ℝ) (hμ : 0 ≤ μ) (hL : 0 < L)
    (α γ : ℕ → ℝ) (x y w v : ℕ → V) (hrun : IsAPGMRun gradh g D μ L α γ x y w v) :
    IsSemiImplicitRun gradh g D μ L α γ x y v := by sorry

end NAGFlow.APGM
